Jasmine Gardosi’s show _Dancing to Music You Hate_ incorporates a mix of beatboxing, poetry, and collaboration with a music band live on stage.
Anxieties of the closet and ‘outness’ are present in earlier parts of the performance of _Dancing to Music You Hate_.
A concluding celebration of gender euphoria is present in _Dancing to Music You Hate_.
The anxieties of the closet and ‘outness’ and the concluding celebration of gender euphoria significantly inform transqueer expression in _Dancing to Music You Hate_.
_Dancing to Music You Hate_ is an award-winning show.
