Title: Intersecting Practices and Traditions in Poetry Performance: Interviews with Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan, Anthony Joseph and Marsha Prescod
URL: https://olh.openlibhums.org/article/id/23434/
Content: ## Abstract

In these interviews, the contemporary poets, Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan, Anthony Joseph and Marsha Prescod, reflect upon their performance practice. They discuss the ways in which their innovative poetry performance and spoken word styles interse

**********Extracted claims**********

Contemporary poets Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan, Anthony Joseph, and Marsha Prescod reflect upon their performance practice in these interviews.
The innovative poetry performance and spoken word styles of Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan, Anthony Joseph, and Marsha Prescod intersect and engage with literary and cultural traditions and art forms.
The engaged art forms include music, story-telling, carnival, the visual arts, history, and politics.
Interviews with performance poets living and working in Britain reveal valuable information about their creative and performance practices.
The interviews were conducted as part of the ‘Poetry Off the Page’ project.
Dr. Julia Lajta-Novak from the University of Vienna directed the ‘Poetry Off the Page’ project.
The ‘Poetry Off the Page’ project was carried out in collaboration with the poetry organisation Apples & Snakes, Goldsmiths University of London, the Centre for Poetry at Queen Mary University of London, and University College Dublin.
The interview format was developed in consultation with Patience Agbabi, Kat François, Amerah Saleh, Benjamin Zephaniah, and Russell Thompson.
Russell Thompson is an archivist from Apples & Snakes.
Apples & Snakes is one of the main organizations promoting spoken word and poetry performance in Britain.
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan is a British spoken word poet, writer, and public educator.
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan was born in Bradford.
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan's parents are second-generation British-Pakistani.
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan grew up in West Yorkshire.
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan studied history at Cambridge University.
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan completed an MA in Postcolonial Studies at SOAS, London.
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan’s poetry has appeared online, on television, and on radio.
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan's poem ‘This Is Not a Humanising Poem’ won second place in the final of the Round House Poetry Slam at the Last Words Festival in London in 2017.
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan’s debut poetry collection, _Postcolonial Banter_, was published with Pluto Press in 2019.
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan’s critical works include _Tangled in Terror: Uprooting Islamophobia_ (2022).
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan’s critical works include _Seeing for Ourselves: And Even Stranger Possibilities_ (2023).
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan has contributed to anti-racist anthologies.
The anti-racist anthologies contributed to by Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan include _I Refuse to Condemn_ (2020) and _Cut from the Same Cloth?_ (2021).
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan is a co-author of _A Fly Girl’s Guide to Univeristy at Cambridge and Other Institutions of Power and Elitism_ (2019).
Odelia Younge, Lola Olufemi, and Audrey Sebatindira are co-authors of _A Fly Girl’s Guide to Univeristy at Cambridge and Other Institutions of Power and Elitism_ (2019).
Suhaiymah Manzoor-Khan’s first full-length play, _Peanut Butter and Blueberries_, premiered at the Kiln Theatre, London in 2024.
_Peanut Butter and Blueberries_ focuses on the lives of two young British Muslims.
Anthony Joseph is a Trinidad-born, London-based poet, musician, novelist, and academic at King’s College London.
Anthony Joseph has released eight albums.
Anthony Joseph’s albums include _Rowing Up River to Get Our Names Back_ (2025).
Anthony Joseph’s albums include _The Rich Are Only Defeated When Running_ (2021).
Anthony Joseph’s albums include _Time_ (2014).
Anthony Joseph’s published verse novels and fictional biographies include _The African Origins of UFOs_ (2006).
Anthony Joseph’s published verse novels and fictional biographies include _The Frequency of Magic_ (2019).
Anthony Joseph’s published verse novels and fictional biographies include _Kitch: A Fictional Biography of a Calypso Icon_ (2018).
Anthony Joseph’s poetry collections include _Desafinado_ (1994).
Anthony Joseph’s poetry collections include _Teragaton_ (1997).
Anthony Joseph’s poetry collections include _Bird Head Son_ (2009).
Anthony Joseph’s poetry collections include _Rubber Orchestras_ (2011).
Anthony Joseph’s poetry collections include _Precious and Impossible: Selected Poems_ (2024).
Anthony Joseph’s poetry collections include _Sonnets for Albert_ (2022).
Anthony Joseph was awarded the T. S. Eliot Prize for _Sonnets for Albert_ in 2023.
Anthony Joseph received the 2023 OCM (One Caribbean Media) Prize for Caribbean Poetry.
Anthony Joseph received the Paul Hamblyn Foundation Composers Award in 2020.
Anthony Joseph received a Jerwood Compton Poetry Fellowship in 2019.
Marsha Prescod appeared at 39 Apples and Snakes Poetry Performances between 1982 and 1997.
