Bowden’s _Commentary on the General Prologue_ stated that Friar Hubert was the perfect epitome of friars as a class.
Bowden’s _Commentary on the General Prologue_ stated that thousands of friars in fourteenth-century England displayed guile and covetousness.
In _The Friars_ (1994), C. H. Lawrence wrote that the allegation that friars let off penitents too lightly was a commonplace of anti-Mendicant polemics.
C. H. Lawrence wrote that this allegation reflected the inability of less educated parish clergy to adapt to the new theology of penance.
