Robert Swanson noted that secular clergy objected that mendicants gave penances which were too light.
Robert Swanson noted that secular clergy rarely complained that people did not confess.
Hagen wrote (1996) that Chaucer closely models his portraits of Friar Huberd and Friar John on the conventions established by the anti-fraternal literary tradition.
